[1m[95m[NARRATION][0m 
  The rain drums against the shutters. A pause hangs between you — long enough 
  for the candle on the table to gutter, for the shadows to shift across Mara's 
  face. She takes a slow breath. Then her right hand moves. She pulls the glove 
  off, finger by finger. Beneath it, a fresh crescent scar cuts across her 
  palm. Pink and puckered. Days old, at most. The wound of something that *bit* 
  deep. She holds her hand out, palm up. Lets you see it in full lamplight. 
  "This is what I found when I went looking for answers about the Ash Gate. 
  Three nights ago. Same night someone tried to force it." Her jaw tightens. "I 
  didn't see who did this. But I saw what they left behind — the scorch marks, 
  the ash that isn't ash. And I saw enough to know I'm not done." She meets 
  your eyes. "I don't make promises lightly, Kael. But I'll make one now." She 
  pulls the glove back on. Tugs it tight. "I'm in. Whatever's behind that gate, 
  whoever's trying to force it open — I'll see it through. You have my word." 
  The reliquary sits between you. The compass is still in your hand. She waits. 
  "So. Where do we start?" 

